# Strimzi Ops — agent instructions

## What this repo is

Ops toolkit for Kafka Connect on Strimzi: connector **lint** (CLI), **monitor**, and **control** (Streamlit UI today).

## Language migration

We are moving from Python to Rust incrementally. Prefer Rust for new shared logic.

1. **Done / in progress:** `strimzi-ops-core` + `strimzi-lint` (lint CLI parity)
2. **Next:** Connect REST client, Kafka monitor, then UI (not RustView for production; prefer Axum+HTMX or similar later)
3. **Until replaced:** keep Python Streamlit/`strimzi_ops` working; do not break `just lint-config` / UI without an equivalent

## Where standards live

- Rust style: [docs/rust-best-practices.md](docs/rust-best-practices.md) — **must follow** [Canonical Rust best practices](https://canonical.github.io/rust-best-practices/introduction.html)
- Cursor rules: `.cursor/rules/` (this file + Rust-specific rules)

## Workspace layout

```
crates/strimzi-ops-core/   # library
crates/strimzi-lint/       # binary CLI
strimzi_ops/               # Python package (legacy during migration)
app.py                     # Streamlit UI
```

## Checks before finishing Rust work

```bash
just rust-check   # fmt + clippy -D warnings
just rust-test
```
